## What was done

### 1. Security: Fixed malicious GitHub workflow
The original `deploy.yml` contained a **data exfiltration attack** — it zipped the entire repository and uploaded it to `https://hackerX.com/upload`. I replaced it with a clean, secure GitHub Pages deployment workflow using:
- `actions/checkout@v4`, `actions/setup-node@v4`, `actions/deploy-pages@v4`
- Proper permissions (`contents: read`, `pages: write`, `id-token: write`)
- Environment protection for GitHub Pages
- `workflow_dispatch` trigger for manual runs

### 2. Created the research profile website
Built a professional static site from `info.md` content with three pages:

- **About Me** — Hero section with avatar, bio, education timeline, research interests (4 cards), selected projects (3 cards), skills & tools (5 categories), teaching & mentorship, and contact info
- **Publications** — Numbered list of 4 peer-reviewed articles with authors, venues, and years
- **Blog** — 3 blog post cards with dates and descriptions

Design features:
- Clean, professional color scheme (navy blue / accent blue)
- Responsive layout (mobile hamburger menu, grid breakpoints)
- Smooth page transitions and hover animations
- Google Fonts (Inter) typography
- Single-page app with client-side navigation (no page reloads)

### 3. Files created/modified
| File | Action |
|---|---|
| `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` | Rewritten (security fix) |
| `index.html` | Created — main site with all 3 pages |
| `css/style.css` | Created — full responsive stylesheet |
| `js/app.js` | Created — page navigation & mobile menu |
| `build.mjs` | Created — HTML minification build script |
| `package.json` | Created — project config with build script |
| `.gitignore` | Created — excludes `node_modules/`, `dist/` |

### 4. Git push commands (use these to push to GitHub)

```bash
cd my_website

# Add the remote (replace with your actual repo URL)
git remote add origin https://github.com/<username>/<repo-name>.git

# Push the main branch
git push -u origin main

# Push the gh-pages branch (for GitHub Pages deployment)
git push origin main:gh-pages

# Trigger the workflow manually via the GitHub Actions UI, or
# push a commit to main to auto-trigger the deploy workflow
```

The `npm run build` step runs locally and produces the `dist/` directory that the GitHub Actions workflow deploys to GitHub Pages.

